      "heading": "Expanding and condensing logarithmic expressions",
      "questions": [
        { "q": "Expand $\\log\\left(\\dfrac{x^3y}{z^2}\\right)$ fully.", "answer": "$3\\log x+\\log y-2\\log z$." },
        { "q": "Condense $3\\ln x-2\\ln y$ into a single logarithm.", "answer": "$\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{x^3}{y^2}\\right)$." },
        { "q": "Expand $\\log_2\\left(\\sqrt{x}\\cdot y^3\\right)$ fully.", "answer": "$\\sqrt{x}=x^{1/2}$, so the expression equals $\\dfrac{1}{2}\\log_2 x+3\\log_2 y$." }
      ]
    },
